{
  "title": "MCP Resources: Share Files and Data with AI Apps | CrestApps for Orchard Core",
  "description": "Resources are files and data that other AI apps can read from your Orchard Core site through the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server. Add a resource once, and every connected AI app reads the current version instead of a pasted copy.\n\nIn this video:\n• Why resources keep AI apps working from current files\n• The resource types: File, Media, FTP/FTPS, SFTP and the Recipe types\n• Adding a File resource with a path placeholder and a MIME type\n• Sharing files of the media library\n• Reading files from an SFTP or FTP server\n• Use cases and sharing with care",
